#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:12
msgid ""
"ZTDeck is a small desktop client for the ZeroTier One service running on "
"your machine. It talks to the local ZeroTier control API, so the daemon "
"keeps doing the networking while ZTDeck gives you a clear view of it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:17
msgid "Features:"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:19
msgid "See your node address, version and online state at a glance"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:20
msgid "Join and leave networks, with network ID validation"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:21
msgid "Copy managed IP addresses to the clipboard"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:22
msgid "Inspect the routes and DNS settings a controller publishes"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:23
msgid ""
"Toggle managed addresses, global routes, default route and DNS per network"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:24
msgid "Inspect peers with their link type and latency"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:25
msgid "Get notified when a network connects or stops responding"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:26
msgid "See when traffic falls back to slow TCP relaying"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:28
msgid ""
"ZTDeck does not bundle the ZeroTier service. Install and start zerotier-one "
"on the host first, then grant your user account read access to the service "
"token as described in the setup screen."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.ygtadk.ZTDeck.metainfo.xml.in.in:33
msgid ""
"This is an unofficial client. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or "
"sponsored by ZeroTier, Inc."
msgstr ""

